*AI Maze Escape (Shortest Path)*
Logic
Represent the maze as a 2D grid.
Treat every empty cell as a node.
Use Breadth First Search (BFS) because every move has equal cost.
Explore neighbouring cells (Up, Down, Left, Right).
Stop when the Goal is reached.
Reconstruct the shortest path.

*Pseudocode*

START

Create Queue
Insert START into Queue
Mark START as Visited

WHILE Queue is not empty

    Remove first node

    IF node is GOAL
        Print path
        STOP

    FOR each neighbour
        IF neighbour is valid AND not visited
            Mark visited
            Store parent
            Insert neighbour into Queue

END WHILE

END
